# Vulnerabilities Trivy is told to walk past, and for how long.
#
# EVERY LINE NEEDS A DATE. An entry with no expiry is not an exception, it is a
# scanner that has been quietly switched off for that CVE forever — and the
# whole reason for scanning is to notice when a base image goes bad six months
# from now.
#
# Format (trivy reads `exp:` natively and starts reporting again after it):
#
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31   # why, and what has to happen before then
#
# Scans already pass --ignore-unfixed, so anything landing here has a patch
# available and was skipped on purpose. Keep this list as short as possible.

# nginx:1.31-alpine, the edge image docker-compose.prod.yml pulls (scanned by
# the `secrets` job). Fixed in Alpine, not yet in any nginx image: 1.31.6
# (2026-09-26) is the newest tag. Remove both lines as soon as a rebuilt
# 1.31-alpine scans clean — or by the date, when CI goes red again and forces it.
# devforge-web is not covered here: its Dockerfile runs `apk upgrade`.
#
# libexpat — /usr/sbin/nginx does not link it (only the fontconfig tools do) and
# no dynamic module is loaded, so the edge never parses XML with it.
CVE-2026-93990 exp:2026-11-06
# pcre2 — nginx links it, but the bug needs a crafted *pattern*; every pattern
# nginx compiles comes from deploy/nginx/devforge.conf, not from requests.
CVE-2026-103111 exp:2026-11-06
